Crash-safe, serialized known_hosts rewrites for Android (no hard links).

Copyright 2026 Sylirre. License: BSD-2-Clause (see Local-patches-LICENSE.txt).
Date: 2026-10-07. Applies to OpenSSH portable 10.5p1 hostfile.c/ssh-keygen.c
together with android-known-hosts.h; non-Android builds are unchanged.

Upstream backs up known_hosts with link() and replaces it with one rename(),
so the live name never disappears. Android app domains cannot hard-link app
data. The previous local patch used rename(file, file.old) + rename(temp,
file), leaving a window with no known_hosts at all (crash => host keys lost,
next connection trusts a new key; readers see ENOENT; a concurrent writer can
move the other's fresh file away). Now: copy-to-temp + fsync + rename for the
backup, fsync + one atomic rename for the new file, fsync of the directory,
and an flock() on "<file>.lock" around every read-modify-write and append.

